-- title:
--   Properness of the two-chart Igusa scheme over ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ (a natural number with the `NeZero` instance) and a prime $\ell$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F$ for the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`. Inside $F$ let `chartAlgFin N ℓ` be the subalgebra of elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by the function `jFull N`, and `chartAlgInf N ℓ` the subalgebra of elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by $(\mathrm{jFull}\ N)^{-1}$; that is, the integral closures of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ and of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. Assume both are of finite type as $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebras. The assertion is that the morphism `igusaTo N ℓ` is proper in the sense of Mathlib's `IsProper`. Here `igusaTo N ℓ` is the morphism from [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255), the pushout of schemes of `fFin N ℓ` and `fInf N ℓ` (the maps on spectra induced by the inclusions `inclFin N ℓ`, `inclInf N ℓ`), to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ obtained by descending the two structure morphisms given by $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` and $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ`, which agree after composition with `fFin N ℓ` and `fInf N ℓ`.
--
--   This is the properness of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, the normalisation of $\mathbb{P}^1_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ in the function field $F$ along the $j$-line, stated here with the finite-type property of the two chart algebras as a hypothesis and with no condition relating $\ell$ to $N$. It supports the constructions of Deligne–Rapoport-style models at a given level, and is used by the level-structure and model-package results on fibres, closed immersions and reducedness that build on this scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_isProper_igusaTo.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Proper

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicGeometry ModularCurve ModularCurve.IgusaScheme

theorem ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isProper_igusaTo (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime]
    [Algebra.FiniteType ↥(GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ) ↥(chartAlgFin N ℓ)]
    [Algebra.FiniteType ↥(GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ) ↥(chartAlgInf N ℓ)] :
    IsProper (igusaTo N ℓ) := by sorry
